From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:42:15 +0300
Subject: Screenshots: declare the grabbed pixels as SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB24

I_GrabScreen returns R,G,B bytes (SDL_RenderReadPixels with SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB24, or
glReadPixels GL_RGB), but I_ScreenShot wrapped them with the masks R=0x0000ff, G=0x00ff00,
B=0xff0000, which describe those bytes only on little-endian: on big-endian the masks make
SDL_PIXELFORMAT_BGR24 and screenshots were saved with red and blue swapped.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/prboom2/src/SDL/i_sshot.c b/prboom2/src/SDL/i_sshot.c
--- a/prboom2/src/SDL/i_sshot.c
+++ b/prboom2/src/SDL/i_sshot.c
@@ -75,8 +75,10 @@ int I_ScreenShot(const char *fname)
 
   if (pixels)
   {
-    screenshot = SDL_CreateRGBSurfaceFrom(pixels, renderW, renderH, 24,
-      renderW * 3, 0x000000ff, 0x0000ff00, 0x00ff0000, 0);
+    // I_GrabScreen's bytes are R,G,B (SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB24, GL_RGB); the masks
+    // 0xff/0xff00/0xff0000 meant that only on little-endian (BGR24 on big-endian)
+    screenshot = SDL_CreateRGBSurfaceWithFormatFrom(pixels, renderW, renderH, 24,
+      renderW * 3, SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB24);
   }
 
   if (screenshot)
